  "notes": "Fields map 1:1 onto the legacy pgAdmin dialog (workflow legacy_preserved): field ids are the BaseUISchema ids and are served by the existing SQL templates. Source: web/pgadmin/browser/server_groups/servers/databases/static/js/database.ui.js (DatabaseSchema, DefaultPrivSchema), static/js/variable.ui.js, static/js/sec_label.ui.js, static/js/privilege.ui.js. pgAdmin Definition fields are mapped by match: encoding/tablespace/collation/ctype/connection limit/template flag->Options, template->General, strategy and locale provider family->Engine; Default Privileges nested tab->Security group; Advanced (schema_res)->Engine; Parameters->Parameters. Field ids are checked against the pgAdmin *.ui.js schema ids by tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_postgresql_schema_ids.py (the schema id gate); the form stays draft until phase 5 routes it to the SQL templates and ports the ui.spec expectations."
